   "slug": "aerospace",
   "name": "Aerospace",
   "restriction": "Export control",
   "restriction_note": "Much of this work is export-controlled. ITAR (22 CFR 120-130) limits access to defense articles and technical data to a 'U.S. person' as defined at 22 CFR 120.62: a citizen, a lawful permanent resident, or a protected individual. This is not a security clearance and it does not require citizenship: a permanent resident qualifies. Someone on a temporary visa is outside that definition, and a license or agreement is then needed to give them access. That temporary-visa population is exactly who IPEDS counts as a non-resident alien.",
   "why": "Airframes, propulsion and spacecraft. The field where the gap between who earns the degree and who the rules admit to the work is widest.",
