 "caveats": [
  "A CIP code is a field of study. Nobody in this data is observed working in the industry it is matched to.",
  "The battery entry is a proxy built from materials programs, because IPEDS publishes no battery category.",
  "Shares are of degrees awarded, not of the current workforce. A doctorate awarded in 2016 may have left the country or the field.",
  "'Non-resident alien' is the IPEDS reporting category: a student on a temporary visa. Permanent residents are counted as domestic.",
  "The restriction note states the law as written. It is not an observed hiring outcome. This data cannot show who was employed, under what authorization, or whether they stayed.",
  "Export control, access authorization and a security clearance are three different things. Only a DOE L or Q access authorization requires US citizenship."
